# Core

`typescript/datasources`, `csharp/Datasources`, and `rust/datasources` hold the shared repository contract. Dialect SQL, quoting, type maps, default-value native text, and serial/identity helpers stay in that provider.

A missing dialect, a compile error, or a copied converter is not a reason to move provider code into core.
